From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:37:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-compositor: the overview's windows and parts: the
 scrolled content alone or the fixed parts alone, with their alpha

T-504 (flags 32 and 64 of jihad_offscreen_compose_post; jihad_offscreen_overview_ok says the engine takes them,
and answers 0 with the swizzle pass, whose shader forces the alpha). The daemon stitches a half-size picture
of the page around a zoom-in point from windows composed at other scrolls, and draws the page's fixed and
stuck parts over it where they sit at the card's new position:
- flag 32, a window: fixed and stuck layers at shadow opacity 0 (their rects still reported, at the window's
  scroll), the frame cleared to transparent black and read with its alpha kept (every other read forces it
  to 0xFF), so the rows no tile covered (past the displayport or the page) read alpha 0 and are left out;
- flag 64, the parts: every leaf layer outside a fixed or stuck one at opacity 0, the same clear and read, so
  the parts come back with their own alpha (see-through sidebars drawn over the new position's content, not
  the old one's);
- both: a fixed sticky probe of 1024 px (every window lists the same sticky layers), and the verify guard now
  keeps the probe's state, so the next real frame does not start from a window's scroll step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XtfxSpM1w2uiVKeLKoV3g3
